Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 21:52:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] (be) fp-walk-specific tests (RBP bounds, slot-busy under
 pause, junk RBP)

Cases 14, 15, 17 from docs/phase2-test-plan.md ship in patches/fp-walk/ rather
than patches/common/ because their fixtures are handler-state mechanics that
only exist in fp-walk:

- case 14 (RbpBoundsRejectOutOfStackRBP) drives `rbp_can_read_for_test`, which
  the common stub does not export.
- case 15 (LateHandlerCannotCorruptNextDumpUnderLoad) pins the handler in the
  fp-walk WALKING state via `pause_handler_for_tid_for_test` and exercises the
  per-sequence ring's CAS rejection; the pause hook is fp-walk-only.
- case 17 (JunkRbpDoesNotCrashCollector) clobbers RBP to an unmapped address
  and dumps, verifying the `mincore` walk guard does not deref it.

Helpers (self_tid, collector_is_stub, ParkedThread, MarkerChain) are
duplicated from native_stack_action_test.cpp because each variant's test file
links independently; the variant write scope is patches/<variant>/ so each
variant carries its own copies. A fresh `FpWalkNativeStackActionTest` fixture
avoids colliding with the common fixture's class name.
